<title>ABU DHABI: Asia-Pacific oil bunker demand to grow - analyst.</title>
<headline>Asia-Pacific oil bunker demand to grow - analyst.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia-Pacific bunker fuel oil consumption, led by Singapore and South Korea, is expected to grow at an annual rate of 3.8 percent between 1995-2000 and 3.4 percent in 2000-2005, an analyst said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This situation translates to bunker fuel oil consumption growth in the Asia-Pacific region from around 580,000 barrels per day (bpd) in 1995 to 690,000 bpd in 2000 and to 810,000 bpd in 2005,&quot; Fereidun Fesharaki, a director at Hawaii-based East-West Center, told delegates at an energy conference here.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect strong growth in bunkering to continue,&quot; Fesharaki said in a conference paper.</p>
<p>Bunker fuel consumption in Singapore was projected to increase at five percent a year during 1995-2000 and four percent in 2000-2005, according to the center.</p>
</text>
